    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-02-24">February 24,
                        1948</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5079"
                            type="person">Mrs. Simmel</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I have received the letter from <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5080" type="person"
                        >Mr. Kaplan</rs> to you about the publications of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1791" type="person">Georg Simmel</rs>&apos;s books
                    in English. The situation is exactly as <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5080"
                        type="person">Mr. Kaplan</rs> describes it and I would not hesitate to write
                    as he asks you to do. I have no copy of my letter to the University Press about
                    this problem.<note type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note> But it may be that <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__5080" type="person">Mr. Kaplan</rs> will receive
                    the text of this part of our agreement from <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2057"
                        type="person">Mr. Fred Wieck</rs>, The University of Chicago Press, 5750
                    Ellis Avenue, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__105" type="place">Chicago</rs>, <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__999" type="place">Ill.</rs></p>
                <p>I<supplied>t</supplied> would be a great satisfaction for all of us if <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1791" type="person">Georg Simmel</rs>&apos;s work
                    which were of great importance to me, would be published in this country.</p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
